## Summary

Two changes, both under the disposable run root:

**`rust/src/lib.rs`** — added the public function:
```rust
pub fn filter_by_tag<'a>(notes: &'a [Note], tag: &str) -> Vec<&'a Note> {
    notes
        .iter()
        .filter(|n| n.tags.iter().any(|t| t == tag))
        .collect()
}
```
Exact match via `==` (not substring), order preserved by `iter().filter()`.

**`rust/src/main.rs`** — wired `--tag <TAG>` into the `list` subcommand: it scans the args after the command for `--tag`, takes the following value as the filter, and passes notes through `notekeep::filter_by_tag` when provided (falling back to all notes otherwise).

Verified: `cargo build` clean, existing `tests/basic.rs` still pass, and end-to-end CLI runs confirm exact-match filtering, order preservation, and the substring guard.


